  "title": "Draft: ftype: Reject time literals without at least hours and minutes",
  "description": "The comments suggest that this is intended, but that's not what the\nbehavior does.\n\nFixup 33adf427aa2e3ddb132735418c04fa34f5e454df\n\nNote the above commit removed parsing of \"date with hours only\".\nFurther note that iso8601_to_nstime also requires at least hours\nand minutes.\n\nPing #21376. This fixes the particular case there - note that since\nthe error only occurred on unquoted strings, it only happened on\ndate-along values, since the non ISO8601 to nstime path doesn't handle\nthe ISO-style \"T\" between the date and time, so it was not possible\nto pass in an unquoted/unescaped literal that would parse with a null\ntimezone and also not allocate extra bytes for the quoting.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
